leds: lcd-backlight duty/div no longer oops; pwm_register removed

store_duty and store_div passed kstrtoul an uninitialised pointer to write the number through:
every write oopsed, then a nested panic rebooted the player (seen 2026-08-30). They now parse with
kstrtouint and reject bad input with -EINVAL. pwm_register wrote any value to any register
address its caller named, through the same broken parser; nothing in Sony's userspace (stock or
Walkman One, system or ramdisk) opens it, so the node is gone.

